00:13:46,950 --> 00:13:47,070
Yeah.

320
00:13:47,250 --> 00:13:47,750
Get up and dance.

321
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:06,420
Stephen, good to see you, brother.

322
00:14:06,880 --> 00:14:07,160
How are you?

323
00:14:07,660 --> 00:14:08,160
How was your trip?

324
00:14:08,760 --> 00:14:09,200
It was fine.

325
00:14:09,920 --> 00:14:11,900
I've been better, but it's great to be home.

326
00:14:12,220 --> 00:14:12,840
I've missed you all.

327
00:14:13,260 --> 00:14:13,680
How's mom?

328
00:14:14,160 --> 00:14:14,620
She's great.

329
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:18,980
All she ever does is talk about you, her little boy that went to United States.

330
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:20,200
You're her pride and joy.

331
00:14:20,520 --> 00:14:21,520
You know that, right?

332
00:14:21,780 --> 00:14:22,980
I can't wait to see you.

333
00:14:23,600 --> 00:14:23,840
You?

334
00:14:24,300 --> 00:14:24,920
What's new with you?

335
00:14:25,700 --> 00:14:27,380
Well, Nisha and I are expecting.

336
00:14:27,380 --> 00:14:30,160
You'll have another nephew or niece soon.

337
00:14:30,930 --> 00:14:31,670
That's great.

338
00:14:32,090 --> 00:14:32,210
Wow.

339
00:14:33,110 --> 00:14:33,510
Congrats.

340
00:14:34,170 --> 00:14:35,390
You two are great together, you know?

341
00:14:35,710 --> 00:14:37,030
You have such a beautiful family.

342
00:14:37,670 --> 00:14:39,170
I hope that one day I can have that.

343
00:14:39,550 --> 00:14:40,290
Of course, man.

344
00:14:40,490 --> 00:14:40,830
Come on.

345
00:14:41,170 --> 00:14:43,850
I mean, everything was set here for you to marry Shalini.

346
00:14:44,600 --> 00:14:46,090
You know, she's still finding after you.

347
00:14:46,520 --> 00:14:47,810
I don't think she'll ever get over you.

348
00:14:48,230 --> 00:14:49,310
What are you talking about?

349
00:14:49,590 --> 00:14:50,390
I hardly knew her.

350
00:14:50,710 --> 00:14:51,790
How could she be in love with me?

351
00:14:52,430 --> 00:14:54,450
I couldn't go through with it even though she's a great woman.

352
00:14:54,830 --> 00:14:56,890
No, I left my heart in the United States.

353
00:14:58,060 --> 00:15:00,200
I just hope Veronica is happy.

354
00:15:00,630 --> 00:15:01,610
Get over it.

355
00:15:01,830 --> 00:15:02,690
You're home now.

356
00:15:03,440 --> 00:15:05,090
Everyone here thinks so highly of you.

357
00:15:05,800 --> 00:15:07,390
They'll be girls throwing themselves at you.

358
00:15:07,600 --> 00:15:08,890
You can marry anyone you want.

359
00:15:09,310 --> 00:15:10,670
I don't want to marry anyone.

360
00:15:11,090 --> 00:15:12,190
I want to marry her.

361
00:15:12,530 --> 00:15:13,270
Don't you understand?

362
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:15,450
You are incorrigible.

363
00:15:18,240 --> 00:15:29,920
Steven, my baby, how are you?

364
00:15:30,060 --> 00:15:31,340
I miss you so much.

365
00:15:31,680 --> 00:15:31,940
Hey, mom.

366
00:15:32,480 --> 00:15:33,200
Great to see you.

367
00:15:33,340 --> 00:15:34,360
You look so thin.

368
00:15:34,880 --> 00:15:36,320
Didn't those Americans feed you?

369
00:15:36,780 --> 00:15:37,260
Come, come.

370
00:15:37,800 --> 00:15:38,800
Let's have some Thai.

371
00:15:39,040 --> 00:15:42,240
By the way, there is a girl here waiting for you.

372
00:15:43,720 --> 00:15:44,100
Hi, Steven.

373
00:15:45,890 --> 00:15:47,930
Veronica, how did you get here?

374
00:15:48,920 --> 00:15:49,840
How do you know where I live?

375
00:15:50,850 --> 00:15:52,970
I waited for you at the airport, but you never showed.

376
00:15:53,610 --> 00:15:58,930
I also have some little secrets that I haven't told you about, but we can discuss that later.

377
00:16:00,170 --> 00:16:05,630
I realized that I was just scared, scared of how much I love you and of the commitment that marriage requires.

378
00:16:06,510 --> 00:16:07,170
I'm here now.

379
00:16:07,690 --> 00:16:09,510
Now, there's something I want to ask you.

380
00:16:10,100 --> 00:16:12,330
Steven, will you marry me?

381
00:16:28,200 --> 00:16:31,000
I now declare you husband and wife.

382
00:16:31,440 --> 00:16:32,340
You may kiss the bride.

383
00:16:38,800 --> 00:16:41,800
Alright, so it's over.

384
00:16:41,800 --> 00:16:43,800
Sad, sad but sweet.

385
00:16:44,390 --> 00:16:44,800
Sad but sweet, huh?

386
00:16:45,730 --> 00:16:48,800
Well, we went from them meeting casually by a bike accident.

387
00:16:49,950 --> 00:16:51,800
Yeah, we had nice music.

388
